5. Breadcrumb UI
When the user clicks into ⁠"10001"⁠, the breadcrumb at the top of the grid should render:
⁠HeadCode: 10001 > Geography⁠
If they click "Back" on the breadcrumb to return to the HeadCode comparison view, simply clear the ⁠filters⁠ array and reset the ⁠dimensions⁠ back to ⁠["HeadCode"]⁠.
Summary for the Frontend Lead
"We moved HeadCode from a hidden backend filter to a first-class visual dimension. Pass the selected head codes in the new root ⁠headCodes⁠ array, start your dimension drill-down at ⁠HeadCode⁠, and when a user clicks a row, append that specific HeadCode to the ⁠filters⁠ array just like you do for Geography or Circle."


